\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Prespecified secondary boundary tests. Event-fraction intervals are Wilson 95\%; final-accuracy intervals are seed-bootstrap 95\%. Changing $p$ changes absolute sample count. Subtraction is an input relabeling of addition. These are not independent confirmations across algorithm families.}}{12}{figure.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:robust}{{5}{12}{Prespecified secondary boundary tests. Event-fraction intervals are Wilson 95\%; final-accuracy intervals are seed-bootstrap 95\%. Changing $p$ changes absolute sample count. Subtraction is an input relabeling of addition. These are not independent confirmations across algorithm families}{figure.5}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Unprojected prediction and oracle-assisted logit diagnostics. Means and seed minima--maxima over the full horizon (step zero is omitted from logarithmic axes). Rule energy subtracts global class bias; residual energy is the orthogonal complement, not a named memorization circuit. These are post hoc diagnostic plots under a predeclared formula, never training signals or deployable projected accuracies.}}{12}{figure.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:diag}{{6}{12}{Unprojected prediction and oracle-assisted logit diagnostics. Means and seed minima--maxima over the full horizon (step zero is omitted from logarithmic axes). Rule energy subtracts global class bias; residual energy is the orthogonal complement, not a named memorization circuit. These are post hoc diagnostic plots under a predeclared formula, never training signals or deployable projected accuracies}{figure.6}{}}
